{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong upward-trend underprediction: when the last 10–15 days show a persistent rise (higher highs/higher lows), add a positive drift to the whole path. The model is systematically too low in rally regimes (often by ~+5 to +15 EUR, growing with horizon).",
    "Horizon-dependent bias: apply a correction that increases with lead time (small adjustment days 1–5, larger days 10–30). Errors compound; the back half of the 30D forecast is most biased low.",
    "Lag/slow regime-switch recognition: after a breakout to new 30-day highs, treat it as a regime change rather than mean reversion. Shift the forecast level upward quickly instead of fading the move.",
    "Over-mean-reversion after dips: when the most recent 3–5 days include a pullback within a broader uptrend, do not project continued weakness; dampen mean reversion and keep the forecast anchored to the rising trendline.",
    "Volatility/convexity miss: in strong trends, increase forecast volatility (wider moves) rather than keeping a flat/sideways profile; the model’s path is too smooth and fails to capture continued acceleration.",
    "Peak/trough timing: the model tends to place local peaks too early and subsequent declines too deep; delay turning points and reduce the magnitude of forecasted drawdowns during bullish regimes."
  ]
}
